    {
      "id": "edge-interaction-selection-task",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Edge Interaction Review",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1612,
        "y": 188
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 520,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "side": "left",
          "offset": 0.2,
          "position": {
            "side": "left",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "side": "top",
          "offset": 0.5,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.5
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "side": "bottom",
          "offset": 0.5,
          "position": {
            "side": "bottom",
            "offset": 0.5
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "side": "left",
          "offset": 0.5,
          "position": {
            "side": "left",
            "offset": 0.5
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "side": "right",
          "offset": 0.5,
          "position": {
            "side": "right",
            "offset": 0.5
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Edge Interaction Review",
        "markdown": "# Edge Interaction Review\n\nEdge selection is currently too weak. Treat hover discovery and selection as separate stages instead of making every edge or edge label aggressively own pointer input.\n\n## Preferred interaction model\n\n1. Ordinary edge: visually present but interaction-light. Canvas behavior should continue to win unless the pointer is deliberately near the edge.\n2. Hover or proximity: highlight the candidate edge and use a modest invisible hit corridor around the rendered path so the user does not have to hit a 1-2 px curve precisely.\n3. Click highlighted edge: select it.\n4. Selected edge: make selection unmistakable and expose appropriate edge actions or relationship controls.\n5. Clicking empty canvas deselects the edge.\n\nEdge labels should normally remain pointer-transparent so they do not create invisible islands that interfere with canvas dragging. An unselected label is presentation only. A hovered edge may highlight its label while the label remains pointer-transparent. A selected edge may allow its label or controls to become interactive when useful.\n\nHover can act as preselection, especially where edges cross or run close together, so the user sees exactly which edge will receive the click before committing.\n\nSemantic zoom should participate. At distant zoom levels, individual edge manipulation may be disabled or reduced because the user is interacting with structure rather than individual relationships.\n\nThe gesture ownership contract should explicitly account for edges so they do not evolve renderer-local event rules. Edge geometry or proximity should discover the target; click establishes selection; selected state exposes interaction.\n\n_Source: exploratory review; not yet committed task scope._",
        "noteKind": "review-commentary",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "interaction-roadmap-declaration"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1786383494774,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "task-node-presentation-density-feedback",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Task Card Presentation Review",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1609,
        "y": 751
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 500,
      "ports": [
