          "dataType": "value",
          "side": "right",
          "offset": 0.5,
          "position": {
            "side": "right",
            "offset": 0.5
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Task Card Presentation Review",
        "markdown": "# Task Card Presentation Review\n\nThe current task-card presentation becomes difficult to read when a task contains substantial work text. This appears primarily to be a class/template presentation issue rather than a problem with the task payload.\n\n## Recommended behavior\n\n1. **Body first:** give the work text substantially more room. Let it expand naturally to a sensible maximum before introducing scrolling or clipping.\n2. **Hide empty metadata:** do not render Target, Started, Completed, Estimate, or similar fields when they have no value.\n3. **Collapse empty sections:** acceptance-hook and other optional regions should not reserve large amounts of space until they contain content.\n4. **Preserve hierarchy:** title and task body should dominate the card. Status, priority, owner, dates, and estimates are secondary information.\n5. **Support semantic presentation levels:** a summary/card view can show title, status, priority, and a short work preview; a detail/editor view can expose the full body, dates, estimate, acceptance hook, external references, and controls.\n\nThe current renderer appears to be presenting detail-view structure at card-view density. Fix the task node class/template rather than shortening individual task data to accommodate the renderer.\n\n_Source: ChatGPT review of the rendered edge-selection note; not yet committed task scope._",
        "noteKind": "review-commentary",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "interaction-roadmap-declaration"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1786383723293,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
